const notes = "<p>Miami-Dade sits on limestone bedrock with a high water table, so many trees have shallow roots and uproot in saturated soil. The county has a tropical climate that allows a huge range of species, from native oaks and gumbo limbo to imported mango, banyan and royal poinciana.</p><p>Hurricane exposure is the biggest factor. Trees that are dead, weakly attached or crowded are the first to fail, so many requests come in before and after the season. Invasive species such as Australian pine and Brazilian pepper are also commonly removed.</p><p>The county's tree rules and those of its many cities differ, so check before cutting. Tell the professional about pools, enclosures and overhead lines when you request an estimate.</p>";

